there is a general realtime  manual
Realtime and Embedded Guide  by Herman Bruyninckx 
<http://www.cs.ru.nl/lab/xenomai/RealtimeAndEmbeddedGuide-Bruyninckx.pdf>
which is pretty good, but is a little bit outdated but the principles 
discussed still hold.


At the radboud university in Nijmegen ( Netherlands) we use xenomai in a 
embedded course.
We have a set of exercises which step by step let you learn xenomai. 
(not everything is handled although)
Each exercise  documents a part of xenomai.

You can find the exercise here :

   http://www.cs.ru.nl/lab/xenomai/
   => click left "exercises" to see the exercises

Currently the old xenomai 2.4 exercises are online, but currently we are 
migrating to xenomai 3 on a raspberry pi 3. So probably next week we 
will replace them with the xenomai 3 exercises. But the first exercises 
are almost similar in xenomai 3 using the alchemy API.

We also supply an image for a raspberry pi 3 ( or any older one) which 
has xenomai cobalt build into the kernel. So If you have an raspberry pi
you can use that to quickly start doing these exercises.


